00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:21.040
And maybe that's why the celeb sensation

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:23.810
surrounding NFTs feels so uncomfortable.

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:26.210
Diet pills might give you the runs,

00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:29.660
but NFTs are a different beast altogether.

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:32.570
At best, they're too new to fully judge

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:36.300
as a major investment and,
at worst, by many accounts,

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:37.880
they're a pyramid scheme.

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:40.090
It's worth noting that
celebrity Ben McKenzie,

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:43.490
aka Ryan from "The OC," is
getting attention lately

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.300
for actually dunking on NFTs.

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:47.950
Welcome to the off chain, (beep)!

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:50.060
But, think about it.

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:51.910
When you buy one of Paris Hilton's

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:53.610
bedazzled boss babe hoodies,

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:57.210
you have a hundred bucks at
stake, which isn't nothing,

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:59.770
but it probably isn't
all of your rent money.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:01.430
But, when she essentially recruits you

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:03.700
by way of a talk show to buy an NFT,

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:06.500
she's doing something else entirely.

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:09.120
See, NFT owners have essentially banked

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.910
on a speculative asset.

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:13.570
If Paris wants to see the
value of that asset grow,

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:14.940
she needs the general public

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.620
to flood the NFT market with capital,

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:20.410
essentially to bolster
her major investment.

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:22.210
And that's where things get tricky.

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:24.840
The allure of feeling like
your lifestyle is closer

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:28.540
to hers or to any rich and
famous person's has the capacity

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:31.960
to wreck your finances and
that's what we're seeing unfold

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:35.280
with Kim Kardashian's
endorsement of EthereumMax.

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.760
It's a developing story
at the time of this video,

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:39.390
but the TLDR is this:

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:41.790
Kim uploaded a sponsored Instagram story

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:44.320
promoting EthereumMax
right after the company

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:47.100
had burned half of
their available Bitcoin.

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:48.190
That means they put them

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:50.400
in an essentially locked crypto wallet

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:52.050
where they can't be distributed.

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:54.910
That created market scarcity,
which drove up the price

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:57.650
for people who were
eager to buy EthereumMax

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:00.310
after being influenced by Kim's story.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:03.560
She and other famous influencers
are currently being sued

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:07.870
because EthereumMax's prices shot up 1300%

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:10.560
before totally crashing a month later.

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:13.830
The lawsuit alleges that it
was a pump and dump scheme.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.030
As far as we can tell,

00:14:15.030 --> 00:14:18.060
the people who bought high
watched their big investments

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:21.400
basically light on fire
in front of their eyes.

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:23.930
But, in addition to being morally dubious,

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:27.680
this whole situation is also
just really, really surreal.

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:30.670
Think about who Paris Hilton
and Kim Kardashian are:

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:33.890
Famous people who literally
invented their celebrity

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:35.298
out of nothing or, that is,

00:14:35.298 --> 00:14:39.040
became famous purely by being seen.

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:41.140
And here they are
endorsing a product that,

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:44.510
by many estimations, is
essentially also made up.

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:47.660
Is this the most meta thing ever? Maybe.

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:50.840
And we think that's best
understood through a concept

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:54.780
from classical political
economy: use value.

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:57.400
See, use value, as the name suggests,

00:14:57.400 --> 00:15:00.070
is a measurement of how
an object derives value

00:15:00.070 --> 00:15:01.450
from its usefulness.

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:03.100
This pair of galoshes?

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:05.490
Great for keeping my feet dry in the rain.

00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:06.480
This spoon?

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:09.210
Excellent for shoveling
cheese whiz into my mouth.

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:12.300
Yeah, I eat cheese is with a
spoon. I'm not a barbarian.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.430
I don't put cans in my mouth.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:17.830
Everything that humans consider
valuable has a use value,

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:20.930
going all the way up to actual people.

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:24.860
The use value of Zendaya for
breaking your heart on screen,

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:28.110
the use value of Doja Cat
for writin' total bangers,

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:29.750
and the use value of Serena Williams

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:32.100
for changing the game of tennis.

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:33.890
When these celebrities endorse things,

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:36.800
there are two use values at play:

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:38.900
that of the celebrity, ie, their fame

00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:40.290
and respective talents,

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.160
and that of the product, say,

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:44.890
the beautifying effects of mascara

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:47.930
or the refreshment of
some Frost Arctic Blitz.

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:50.160
But, for celebs like Paris and Kim,

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:53.480
their fame is a purely ephemeral commodity

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:55.560
with no obvious use value.

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:58.480
Their celebrity isn't linked
to tangible talents beyond,

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:02.460
you know, sharing really
innovative thoughts on work ethic.

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:04.180
- Get your (beep) ass up and work.

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:06.830
- And this is where
things get even more meta.

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:08.960
Marxist economics talks about what happens

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:11.690
when a commodity's value becomes detached

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:15.220
from the actual thing that
can be bought, sold or traded.

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:17.200
Like when a pair of Nikes becomes less

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.070
about helping you avoid ankle sprains

00:16:19.070 --> 00:16:21.250
and more about what it represents:

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:23.680
the fearlessness of Serena Williams.

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:24.513
In this way,

00:16:24.513 --> 00:16:28.140
the commodity essentially
becomes a theological entity,

00:16:28.140 --> 00:16:30.720
something that transcends use value.

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:32.680
It's now a spiritual thing

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:35.000
with what one German economist called

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:38.610
metaphysical subtleties
and theological niceties.

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:40.330
So, we have two things.

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:43.330
One, celebrities without
use value or celebrities

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:44.530
that have been constructed out

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:47.190
of thin air using their clout to push,

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:50.720
two, NFTs, which have a use value

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:54.430
that's arguably also
constructed out of thin air.

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:55.990
The whole thing starts to feel

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:58.200
like a digital house of cards.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:00.230
If celebrities who have value simply

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:03.330
for having value are now
pushing digital commodities

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:06.840
that also have value
simply for having value,

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:08.450
it seems like maybe we're all

00:17:08.450 --> 00:17:11.200
just emperors without any clothes.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:12.750
But, what do you guys think?

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:14.480
If it brings someone actual joy

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:16.740
to feel like they are a
player in the marketplace

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:19.410
on par with Paltrow or Eric Andre,

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:21.080
is there really any harm in it?

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:23.540
Should we just let people enjoy things

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:25.830
and say a little prayer
that it doesn't lead

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:27.250
to their financial ruin?

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:30.120
And, if it does, should
celebrities feel bad about that

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:31.860
or even be held accountable?

